remotely-hellofresh:greenhouse:7926689.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior, Product Validation Technologist&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Factor_ &lt;/strong&gt;a brand of HelloFresh is seeking a Senior, Product Validation Technologist&amp;nbsp;to join the Product Validation team. The Product Validation Technologist III will be responsible for the planning, execution and reporting of validation testing for new ingredients, equipment, recipe builds and product launches. You will also be responsible for the preparation and successful execution of recipe commercialization &amp;amp; development of ingredient specifications in-line with Factor objectives. To thrive in this role you will need to have a genuine interest in utilizing data and metrics to find food manufacturing optimization and improvement opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will ...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee daily workload allocation and utilization for the on-site Ingredient Solutions team, ensuring consistent project coverage and team productivity. When capacity exists, coordinate with partner teams (Commercialization and Kitchen Excellence) to identify additional projects that keep the team engaged and aligned with company priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, execute, and capture data on Recipe Scaling tests to assist in guiding operations and production needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute validation testing of new ingredients and equipment in line with cross-functional team needs and company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize,conduct &amp;amp; report sensory evaluations of new ingredients and recipes with internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise between Operations, Culinary, Procurement and Nutrition teams to help bring company initiatives to completion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the development and maintaining of company specifications, SOPs, and best practices in regard to product and supplier onboarding.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an understanding of production process to assist in identifying process and evaluation improvement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate finished products to validate end-customer experience and shelf-life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor members of to help them maximize their effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are ....&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented - You are able to schedule, organize and execute detailed testing plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;self-driven, goal oriented, and interested in continued learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;strong in verbal and written communication, able to generate report on product testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;able to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;able to handle multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;able to lift up to 50 lbs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At a minimum, you have ...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An undergraduate degree in Food Science, Culinary Science, Biology, Chemistry or a related science field or Culinary Arts background with 3+ years of culinary experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 - 3+ years’ experience in food manufacturing, food product development, applications, operations or applicable culinary experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a proficiency in MS Office and/or Google Suite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;experience in utilizing basic analytical, pilot and culinary equipment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll get…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, 401k with company match that vest immediately upon participation, and company equity plan based on role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous PTO, including sabbatical, and parental leave of up to 16 weeks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Comprehensive health and wellness benefits with options at $0 monthly, effective first day of employment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Tuition reimbursement for continuing education (upon 2 years of service)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Up to 85% discount on subscriptions to HelloFresh meal plans (HelloFresh, Green Chef, Everyplate, and Factor_)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Access to 7 different Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) including those for BIPOC, women, veterans, parents, and LGBTQ+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Inclusive, collaborative, and dynamic work environment within a fast-paced, mission-driven company that is disrupting the traditional food supply chain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job description is intended to provide a general overview of the responsibilities. However, the Company reserves the right to adjust, modify, or reassign work tasks and responsibilities as needed to meet changing business needs, operational requirements, or other factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#Factor #JD1008&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Illinois Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$74,813&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$83,125 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

rethinkcapital-vivvi:greenhouse:76433830.descriptionHtml:
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;235&quot; data-end=&quot;329&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;235&quot; data-end=&quot;248&quot;&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Liberty, NC&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;331&quot; data-end=&quot;345&quot;&gt;Who We Are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;346&quot; data-end=&quot;726&quot;&gt;Vivvi is reimagining child care and early learning! We’re not your typical daycare or preschool—we create modern, supportive, and fun learning environments where children and teachers thrive. Vivvi is proud to partner with Toyota to provide exceptional enrichment and child care for school-aged children (ages 6–12) during spring and summer breaks on the Liberty, NC campus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;728&quot; data-end=&quot;746&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;747&quot; data-end=&quot;792&quot;&gt;As a School Age Head Teacher, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;793&quot; data-end=&quot;1369&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;793&quot; data-end=&quot;910&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;795&quot; data-end=&quot;910&quot;&gt;Lead and facilitate engaging lessons, enrichment activities, and after-school programs for children ages 6–12&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;911&quot; data-end=&quot;1008&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;913&quot; data-end=&quot;1008&quot;&gt;Supervise and guide cohorts of up to 17 children, ensuring safety, structure, and inclusivity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1009&quot; data-end=&quot;1114&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1011&quot; data-end=&quot;1114&quot;&gt;Build a positive, nurturing, and fun environment that fosters learning, creativity, and curiosity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1115&quot; data-end=&quot;1222&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1117&quot; data-end=&quot;1222&quot;&gt;Develop trusting relationships with children, families, and colleagues through consistent communication&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1223&quot; data-end=&quot;1302&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1225&quot; data-end=&quot;1302&quot;&gt;Apply positive behavior management strategies with empathy and patience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1303&quot; data-end=&quot;1369&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1305&quot; data-end=&quot;1369&quot;&gt;Follow and uphold all health, safety, and program policies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;1371&quot; data-end=&quot;1397&quot;&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1398&quot; data-end=&quot;1958&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1398&quot; data-end=&quot;1482&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1400&quot; data-end=&quot;1482&quot;&gt;Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in Education, Early Childhood, or related field&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1483&quot; data-end=&quot;1584&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1485&quot; data-end=&quot;1584&quot;&gt;1–2 years of experience leading school-age classrooms, summer camps, or after-school programs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1585&quot; data-end=&quot;1676&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1587&quot; data-end=&quot;1676&quot;&gt;Passion for working with children ages 6–12 and seeing each child as capable and unique&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1677&quot; data-end=&quot;1756&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1679&quot; data-end=&quot;1756&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of child development and age-appropriate practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1757&quot; data-end=&quot;1820&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1759&quot; data-end=&quot;1820&quot;&gt;Flexible, creative, and able to adapt activities on the fly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1821&quot; data-end=&quot;1874&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1823&quot; data-end=&quot;1874&quot;&gt;Team-oriented with excellent communication skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1875&quot; data-end=&quot;1958&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1877&quot; data-end=&quot;1958&quot;&gt;Commitment to safety, health protocols, and inclusive learning environments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;1960&quot; data-end=&quot;1985&quot;&gt;Why You’ll Love Vivvi&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1986&quot; data-end=&quot;2256&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1986&quot; data-end=&quot;2049&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1988&quot; data-end=&quot;2049&quot;&gt;Meaningful work in a supportive, innovative environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2050&quot; data-end=&quot;2123&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2052&quot; data-end=&quot;2123&quot;&gt;Opportunities to lead, design activities, and grow professionally&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2124&quot; data-end=&quot;2184&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2126&quot; data-end=&quot;2184&quot;&gt;Collaborative team that values your creativity and ideas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2185&quot; data-end=&quot;2256&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2187&quot; data-end=&quot;2256&quot;&gt;Direct impact on children’s learning, curiosity, and confidence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2258&quot; data-end=&quot;2357&quot;&gt;Ready to make a difference this spring and summer? Apply today and join Vivvi in Liberty, NC!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;2359&quot; data-end=&quot;2362&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Competitive Compensation and Benefits&lt;/em&gt;: &lt;em&gt;Competitive Compensation and Benefits&lt;/em&gt;: Our camp counselors earn hourly rates based on level of education and experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Child-Centered Approach:&lt;/em&gt; Our Camp Director facilitates each child’s success by observing their interests and developing activities inspired by their curiosity. Learn more about our teaching philosophy here https://vivvi.com/programs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;State-of-the-Art Facilities&lt;/em&gt;: All of our environments are purposefully designed to offer endless opportunities for learning and discovery and the brand new, state-of-the-art Liberty campus is your playground for this summer program. The camp will have access to the most up-to-date materials and equipment to ensure counselors have everything they need to deliver a high-quality educational experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Employee Development&lt;/em&gt;: We offer robust training and individual feedback. We also love to promote and hire from within and are committed to helping our colleagues achieve their career goals at Vivvi.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;To be considered, applicants must be based in or willing to relocate to Liberty, N.C. Candidates must also possess independent US work authorization. Physical demands of this position include but are not limited to sitting and standing for extended periods, bending at the waist, reaching overhead, and frequently moving or lifting children weighing up to 50 pounds unassisted. Applicants requiring reasonable accommodation should contact hr@vivvi.com. Determinations will be made on a case-by-case basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, or other characteristics protected by state or federal law or local ordinance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2392&quot; data-end=&quot;2740&quot;&gt;Index: school-age teacher, head teacher school age, summer camp teacher, after-school program, child care teacher, elementary enrichment, Liberty NC teaching jobs, school-aged enrichment programs, school-aged learning, youth enrichment, school-age classroom leader, children ages 6-12, early learning teacher, summer teaching jobs, Liberty NC child care&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2392&quot; data-end=&quot;2740&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keywords:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; &lt;em&gt;school age teacher, after school teacher, afterschool teacher, summer camp counselor, summer camp teacher, youth program leader, child care teacher, childcare provider, elementary enrichment teacher, enrichment instructor, youth development specialist, school age childcare, before and after school care, school age program leader, classroom leader (ages 6-12), children ages 6-12, elementary education jobs, early childhood education jobs, summer teaching jobs, seasonal teaching jobs, part-time teaching jobs, camp counselor jobs near me, child care jobs near me, Liberty NC teaching jobs, Liberty NC child care jobs, after school programs, youth enrichment programs, hands-on learning, experiential learning, behavior management, classroom management, positive guidance, child development, flexible teaching jobs, entry-level education jobs, education careers, teaching opportunities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions? Reach out to us at hr@vivvi.com and include your resume. We look forward to receiving and reviewing your application!&lt;/p&gt;

riverparkvc-via-2-2fb20cbb-5525-40ba-98d.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;Via is on a mission to create public transportation systems that provide far greater access to jobs, healthcare, and education. Our platform serves as the technology backbone for modern transit networks, transforming antiquated and siloed public transportation systems into smart, data-driven, and efficient digital networks. With hundreds of agency partners around the world, Via is recognized as the leading transportation technology and service provider globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;City Operations Manager &lt;/strong&gt;at Via, you will lead the day-to-day operations of two on-demand mobility services in the Dingolfing-Landau and Mühldorf districts. You’ll ensure passengers are reliably transported while driving continuous improvements and operational excellence. This role offers a unique opportunity to shape the future of rural mobility, work closely with drivers and local teams, and make a tangible impact on communities that rely on efficient, reliable public transport.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is also referred to internally as &quot;Field Manager&quot;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the heart of operations for our public transport services - &lt;a href=&quot;https://ridewithvia.com/de/ressourcen/landi&quot;&gt;“LanDi”&lt;/a&gt; in Dingolfing and the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.muehldorf.de/111-Verkehr.html&quot;&gt;“Rufbus”&lt;/a&gt; in Mühldorf - serving as the primary point of contact and operational leader for our drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take full ownership of day-to-day service delivery, ensuring passengers are reliably transported while closely monitoring key performance metrics and operational outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop your team by managing onboarding, mentoring drivers, and ensuring efficient shift planning that keeps services running smoothly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Via’s central operations teams to identify opportunities to improve service quality and implement process optimization initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring your ideas and operational expertise to continuously enhance the rider and driver experience, helping make our mobility services in the region better every single day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading operational teams, ideally in environments with shift-based staff or frontline operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable being on-site regularly (at least 3 days per week) to work closely with drivers and support day-to-day operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills and a calm, solutions-oriented mindset when navigating operational challenges with drivers or external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven approach to problem solving, using performance metrics to guide decisions and improve outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated by fast-paced environments and excited to implement ideas that improve processes and service quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills at C1 level or higher and English at B2 level or higher.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid Class B driver’s license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Becoming part of a company that was awarded for its commitment to social good.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: between €40,000 and €55,000 per year. Final salary will be determined by the candidate’s experience, knowledge, and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Urban Sports Club membership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension scheme (bAV) with a 20% employer contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 vacation days a year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There has never been a more exciting time to be on the cutting edge of public mobility. Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
